 "transcript": [
  "[action] (to the eldest son, the second son) Wang Lung speaks to his sons, asking about their duties.",
  "[action] The eldest son and the second son bow in reply to their father.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"Well, and what is it you are about, then?\"",
  "[silence] Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "the eldest son: \"Well, and what is it you are about, then?\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung turns and goes back to the kitchen.",
  "[says] (to Wang Lung) The eldest son scolds his father for not letting him choose his own wife.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"And you must choose her yourself if you will---if you can---any woman you wish in the town if you have the money to give her.\"",
  "[action] (to the second son) The eldest son scolds his father for not letting him choose his wife.",
  "the eldest son (to the second son): \"Well, and I will choose my wife myself, and you shall choose yours yourself.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and I suppose I have no right to stop you---if you can---any man in this house---\"",
  "[says] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung says he will stop them if they do not have the means.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"if you cannot afford to marry a woman, I will not have you marry at all.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and I suppose you will have your way if you can manage it.\"",
  "[says] (to the second son) The eldest son says he will marry and raise sons.",
  "the eldest son (to the second son): \"Well, and I will marry and raise sons and daughters, and they shall be good and shall do well and you shall have a good wife and good sons and daughters and so you shall.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and if you are determined to do as you like, I will not stand in your way---only do what is fitting, my son.\"",
  "[action] The eldest son leaves with his wife and children.",
  "[action] (to Wang Lung) The eldest son scolds his father.",
  "[says] (to Wang Lung) The eldest son scolds his father for not being as rich as he is."
